# Tauri desktop/iOS project — Rust build artifacts (src-tauri/target, 4.6GB+)
# and the generated Xcode/iOS scaffolding (src-tauri/gen). None of this is part
# of the Vercel web deploy, and watching its ~17k files makes `vercel dev` hit
# EMFILE (too many open files) on macOS. Excluding it keeps the dev watcher and
# deploy uploads to the actual web app.
src-tauri

# Desktop release notes / changelog inputs that aren't needed by the web build
RELEASE_NOTES.md

# Vercel turns EVERY file under api/ into a deployed serverless function, so a
# colocated test would ship as a live public endpoint — api/pages/interpret.test.ts
# becomes /api/pages/interpret.test. (Tests under api/_lib/ are already excluded:
# Vercel skips underscore-prefixed directories.) Verified by inspecting
# .vercel/output/functions after `vercel build`.
api/**/*.test.ts
